s of  votes to determine which course to  pursue crucially the government stands  ready to abide by the decision of the  house but to make this process work the  opposition would need to agree to this  too the government would then bring  forward the withdrawal agreement bill we  would want to agree a timetable for this  bill to ensure it is passed before the  22nd of May so that the United Kingdom  need not take part in European  parliamentary elections this is a  difficult time for everyone passions are  running high on all sides of the  argument but we can and must find the  compromises that will deliver what the  British people voted for this is a  decisive moment in the story of these  islands and it requires national unity  to deliver the national interest
 

